<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-S1-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-S1-002" ;
  triage:title "AtmProtocol import and codec field unused on Windows — Windows CI lint failure (atm/src/composition.rs:15,116)" ;
  triage:description "atm/src/composition.rs:15 — `use atm_core::boundary::{AtmProtocol, ClientTransport}` imports AtmProtocol which is unused on Windows because the unix code path that consumes it is gated. atm/src/composition.rs:116 — `codec: JsonAtmProtocolCodec` struct field never read on Windows path. Both produce Windows CI lint errors. Confirmed still open at c0a0149 by S.1 QA-4 CI run 25594655768. Fix: gate the AtmProtocol import under #[cfg(unix)] and gate the codec field declaration and initialization under #[cfg(unix)]. Same pattern already applied in atm-daemon. (quality-mgr reported as CI-BLOCK-002-S1 in S.1 QA-3 report; confirmed STILL_OPEN in S.1 QA-4 report.)" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
